WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:10.220
A new Fordham Institute study reported
that 28% of teachers in traditional

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.230
district schools use personal leave and
sick days

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:17.609
to miss more than two weeks of school
each year. And anyone who's spent any time

00:00:17.609 --> 00:00:22.230
in school knows that little gets done
when substitutes are in charge. Teachers

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:26.039
unions could have acknowledged the
problem and pledged to tackle it. Instead

00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:30.000
they offered a litany of excuses! One
union leader said the study was

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.940
"motivated by an anti-student agenda".
Another termed it "ideological propaganda".

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:40.140
The president of the nation's largest
teachers union said it was "misguided to

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.550
think that teachers are missing too much
time". Now let's be fair: teaching has its

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:48.600
upsides, but it's a tough profession.
Teachers are on their feet for hours at

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.829
a stretch. If they feel dizzy or down,
they can't just take a long lunch or

00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:56.390
knock off early. Teachers can't even go
to the bathroom when they want!

00:00:56.390 --> 00:01:00.690
Acknowledging all of that is absolutely
in order, yet it will be hard for

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:05.040
teachers to earn the professional esteem
they seek until those who claim to speak

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.620
for their profession start to grow up.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.940
To learn more about my take on the role of

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:16.320
teachers unions, check the links in the
description below. Also, let us know what

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.030
other topics you'd like our scholars to
cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:26.689
and subscribe for more research and
videos from AEI.

